\subsection{\textcolor{black}{Comparison with Recent Authentication Systems (2020--2026)}}\label{sec:recent}
This work presents an end to end multimodal biometric authentication system and therefore, the comparison is restricted to recent studies that explicitly implement a biometric authentication or verification procedure. Table~\ref{tab:recentsec} compares the proposed scheme with five relevant authentication systems published between 2024 and 2026 \cite{jha2024featurefusion,aanjankumar2025smartcity,jha2025ensemble,chen2026twostep,jha2025challenge}. Works primarily focused on biometric recognition, presentation attack detection, cross-modal attacks, or template protection techniques \cite{alharbi2023facevoice,mandalapu2021avpad,jiang2024foice,rathgeb2023btp,zhao2023deephash} are considered supporting literature rather than directly comparable authentication systems. In Table~\ref{tab:recentsec}, \checkmark\ denotes a property that is supported or present, whereas \xmark\ denotes a property that is not supported, not implemented, or outside the scope of the corresponding system. For the proposed system, ``challenge only'' denotes challenge response evidence rather than a dedicated Presentation Attack Detection or deepfake detector.

